WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.466
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level B two.

2
00:00:05.766 --> 00:00:09.396
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.696 --> 00:00:15.751
Unit twenty-four: Compound Adjectives. Today you will build adjectives with hyphens.

4
00:00:16.051 --> 00:00:18.691
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:19.633 --> 00:00:22.947
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:23.783 --> 00:00:24.657
Well-known.

7
00:00:25.650 --> 00:00:27.313
Well-known means famous.

8
00:00:27.917 --> 00:00:29.429
A well-known singer.

9
00:00:30.017 --> 00:00:32.402
Your turn. Say: Well-known.

10
00:00:35.267 --> 00:00:36.488
Well-known.

11
00:00:37.250 --> 00:00:38.228
Long-term.

12
00:00:39.217 --> 00:00:41.704
Long-term means lasting a long time.

13
00:00:42.317 --> 00:00:44.072
A long-term plan.

14
00:00:44.683 --> 00:00:47.417
Your turn. Say: Long-term.

15
00:00:50.267 --> 00:00:51.442
Long-term.

16
00:00:52.183 --> 00:00:53.219
Hard-working.

17
00:00:54.217 --> 00:00:56.344
Hard-working means working with effort.

18
00:00:56.950 --> 00:00:58.613
A hard-working student.

19
00:00:59.217 --> 00:01:01.637
Your turn. Say: Hard-working.

20
00:01:04.500 --> 00:01:05.664
Hard-working.

21
00:01:06.417 --> 00:01:07.511
Part-time.

22
00:01:08.517 --> 00:01:10.830
Part-time means for only some hours.

23
00:01:11.417 --> 00:01:12.940
A part-time job.

24
00:01:13.550 --> 00:01:15.970
Your turn. Say: Part-time.

25
00:01:18.833 --> 00:01:19.800
Part-time.

26
00:01:20.550 --> 00:01:21.656
Five-star.

27
00:01:22.650 --> 00:01:25.033
Five-star means of the highest rating.

28
00:01:25.617 --> 00:01:27.291
A five-star hotel.

29
00:01:27.883 --> 00:01:30.826
Your turn. Say: Five-star.

30
00:01:33.667 --> 00:01:35.318
Five-star.

31
00:01:36.083 --> 00:01:37.282
Old-fashioned.

32
00:01:38.283 --> 00:01:40.376
Old-fashioned means not modern.

33
00:01:40.983 --> 00:01:42.600
An old-fashioned shop.

34
00:01:43.183 --> 00:01:45.708
Your turn. Say: Old-fashioned.

35
00:01:48.567 --> 00:01:49.835
Old-fashioned.

36
00:01:50.583 --> 00:01:51.561
Hyphen.

37
00:01:52.550 --> 00:01:55.490
Hyphen means the sign - joining words.

38
00:01:56.083 --> 00:01:57.259
Use a hyphen.

39
00:01:57.850 --> 00:02:00.166
Your turn. Say: Hyphen.

40
00:02:03.000 --> 00:02:03.827
Hyphen.

41
00:02:04.583 --> 00:02:05.666
Adjective.

42
00:02:06.650 --> 00:02:08.870
Adjective means a describing word.

43
00:02:09.483 --> 00:02:10.647
An adjective.

44
00:02:11.250 --> 00:02:13.717
Your turn. Say: Adjective.

45
00:02:16.567 --> 00:02:17.719
Adjective.

46
00:02:18.533 --> 00:02:22.091
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:22.950 --> 00:02:26.261
Visal, describe yourself with two compound adjectives.

48
00:02:27.350 --> 00:02:41.612
I am a hard-working and open-minded student. A compound adjective is two or more words joined by a hyphen, working as one adjective before a noun.

49
00:02:42.717 --> 00:02:44.031
What are the patterns?

50
00:02:45.117 --> 00:03:01.880
Adjective + noun + -ed: kind-hearted. Number + noun: a five-star hotel, a ten-minute walk. Adverb + participle: well-known, newly built. Noun + participle: hand-made.

51
00:03:02.983 --> 00:03:04.286
What about the plural?

52
00:03:05.383 --> 00:03:18.914
The noun inside a number compound stays singular: a ten-minute walk, not a ten-minutes walk. We write a hyphen before a noun but not after the verb: The singer is well known.

53
00:03:20.067 --> 00:03:21.497
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:22.350 --> 00:03:26.056
Grammar focus: Compound adjectives with hyphens.

55
00:03:26.356 --> 00:03:27.659
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:28.350 --> 00:03:30.164
She is a hard-working student.

57
00:03:31.050 --> 00:03:33.003
We stayed in a five-star hotel.

58
00:03:33.917 --> 00:03:36.195
It was a ten-minute walk.

59
00:03:37.133 --> 00:03:45.152
Join two words with a hyphen before a noun. Number compounds are singular: a ten-minute walk. After be, we often omit the hyphen.

60
00:03:45.917 --> 00:03:48.697
Be careful! Don't say: A ten-minutes walk.

61
00:03:50.633 --> 00:03:53.237
Say: A ten-minute walk.

62
00:03:53.537 --> 00:03:54.956
Keep the noun singular.

63
00:03:55.767 --> 00:03:58.419
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:59.233 --> 00:04:00.629
Words Joined Together.

65
00:04:00.929 --> 00:04:04.299
My sister is a hard-working and kind-hearted person.

66
00:04:05.300 --> 00:04:08.693
We stayed in a five-star hotel near the beach.

67
00:04:09.700 --> 00:04:12.257
It was only a ten-minute walk to the market.

68
00:04:13.267 --> 00:04:16.091
He has a part-time job and a long-term plan.

69
00:04:17.100 --> 00:04:19.796
The old-fashioned shop sells well-known brands.

70
00:04:20.900 --> 00:04:24.658
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:25.517 --> 00:04:26.912
It was a blank walk.

72
00:04:27.212 --> 00:04:32.282
A, ten-minutes. B, ten-minute. C, ten minute's.

73
00:04:35.833 --> 00:04:37.914
The answer is B: ten-minute.

74
00:04:39.050 --> 00:04:41.955
She works only some hours; she has a blank job.

75
00:04:42.255 --> 00:04:46.094
A, part-time. B, full-time. C, long-time.

76
00:04:49.633 --> 00:04:51.412
The answer is A: part-time.

77
00:04:52.550 --> 00:04:54.979
A person who works with effort is blank.

78
00:04:55.279 --> 00:04:59.072
A, hard-working. B, well-known. C, old-fashioned.

79
00:05:02.633 --> 00:05:04.784
The answer is A: hard-working.

80
00:05:05.950 --> 00:05:08.077
Which uses the hyphen correctly?

81
00:05:08.377 --> 00:05:15.084
A, a five star hotel. B, a five-star hotel. C, a five-stars hotel.

82
00:05:18.633 --> 00:05:21.434
The answer is B: a five-star hotel.

83
00:05:22.583 --> 00:05:25.814
According to the reading, what sells well-known brands?

84
00:05:26.114 --> 00:05:30.138
A, the shop. B, the hotel. C, the market.

85
00:05:33.700 --> 00:05:35.769
The answer is A: the shop.

86
00:05:36.967 --> 00:05:40.049
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:40.883 --> 00:05:44.044
Describe yourself using two compound adjectives.

88
00:05:52.850 --> 00:05:54.350
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:05:54.650 --> 00:06:07.743
I am a hard-working and open-minded student with a long-term goal. I want a well-paid job in the future. Each compound adjective joins two words with a hyphen.

90
00:06:08.043 --> 00:06:09.775
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:06:10.683 --> 00:06:15.576
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and compound adjectives with hyphens.

92
00:06:15.876 --> 00:06:20.375
Today's value is diligence. Check the details carefully before you commit.

93
00:06:20.675 --> 00:06:23.513
See you in Unit twenty-five. Goodbye!

94
00:06:23.813 --> 00:06:26.442
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

